// §14 entry 12 -- a capability-bearing implementation constructed behind a
// bare `dyn` -> EXS-E0510.
//
// §4.4: "`dyn Trait poscit P`. Constructing a trait object from an
// implementation whose mark exceeds `P` is EXS-E0510." A bare `dyn Trait`
// (no `poscit` at all) is bound to the EMPTY row, so ANY capability-bearing
// implementation exceeds it. §4.3's own example: "A type with a
// capability-typed field, transitively, is capability-bearing... structura
// ScriptorRetis { sock: rete } // capability-bearing: [rete]" -- reused
// directly below.
//
// §4.4 also names the reason this should be rare rather than common: "a
// file writer's authority IS the handle in its field... If you need [a
// `poscit` on a trait method], the capability is probably misplaced" -- the
// violation here is not that `Scriptor` (the trait) declares a `poscit`; it
// is that erasing `ScriptorRetis` into a BARE `dyn Scriptor` throws away the
// `[rete]` mark that made it capability-bearing in the first place, which is
// exactly what would "hide capabilities from the audit" (§10.3) if allowed.
//
// The exact surface syntax for an `impl` block associating `ScriptorRetis`
// with `Scriptor` is not attested anywhere in the spec text read for this
// suite (§4, §5 and their examples show trait/struct declarations and
// capability rows, never a full `impl Trait for Type` block) -- represented
// here as best-effort rather than invented wholesale; the load-bearing part
// of this fixture is the LAST line, converting a capability-bearing value
// into a bare (empty-row) `dyn Scriptor`.
//
// DEFERRED: needs the capability-bearing-type tracker and `dyn` bound
// checker (§4), which needs the type checker (Stage 2).
// compiler/x86_64/ast/ and cst/ are both still empty; `exsc aedifica`, run
// directly against this file, exits 0 and reports nothing -- confirmed,
// not assumed.

interfacies Scriptor {
    functio scribe(t: textus) -> mensura
}

structura ScriptorRetis { sock: rete }

publica functio erade_potestatem(s: ScriptorRetis) -> dyn Scriptor {
    redde s
}

// TEST: entry=12 shape=code expect-code=EXS-E0510 status=deferred needs=capability_checker
